When the control signal \(A = 1\) and \(\overline{A} = 0\), both nMOS and pMOS transistors conduct, allowing the input signal to pass directly to the output. 
When \(A = 0\) and \(\overline{A} = 1\), both transistors are OFF, isolating the input from the output and resulting in a high-impedance state.








